      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NYACK (2) comes off his first Group 1 victory in the Len Smith Mile at Menangle last week where he charged through a gap on the pegs to win by 4m. Deserved that after placing in both the Victoria Cup and the Inter Dominion Final earlier this season, the latter at this circuit. Has the speed to take advantage of the low draw and his record at this distance range is strong so he can strike again. DANGEROUS (3) was 11 metres behind NYACK when fifth in the Len Smith Mile but he did draw wide and had to work to get to the front. Much better drawn and is two from two at this distance range so can bridge that gap. CAPTAIN SHUFFLES (10) continues to race well having come from this row to place in both outings since winning at this circuit and distance. With even luck he can make an impact. ATTACHMENT (6) had to work last start but has a good record at this circuit and distance including a win two back while DASHING (1) has had tougher barriers of late so could be an improver from the ace draw.",
